    "answer_markdown": "IOVA: ## Iovance Biotherapeutics (IOVA): Forward-Looking Research Brief **Company and catalyst.** Iovance sells Amtagvi, a tumor-infiltrating lymphocyte (TIL) cell therapy for advanced melanoma. As of Oct 15, 2026, IOVA was up about 43.7% in one month, 185.6% in three months, and 543.4% over one year. The reported trigger for the latest leg: Iovance raised its full-year 2026 revenue guidance to $410\u2013420 million from $350\u2013370 million, citing strong Amtagvi demand and improving manufacturing; shares surged over 31% to a fresh multi-year high ([Perplexity Finance](https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/IOVA?comparing=IOVA,FATE,BLRX,GERN,ADAPY,RCKT); [Yahoo Finance](https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/IOVA/)). On Oct 14, 2026 the stock closed at $14.21, down 2% that day after the surge ([Heygotrade](https://www.heygotrade.com/en/us-stock/iova/)). Quarterly fundamentals back the growth story: Q2 2026 revenue was $99.31 million, up 65.7% year over year; net loss narrowed to $47.3 million from $111.7 million a year earlier; operating cash flow was -$60.8 million. The balance sheet shows $736.0 million of stockholders' equity against $179.5 million of total liabilities. A simple check of the guidance: first-half 2026 revenue was $170.7 million ($71.4M + $99.3M). To reach the low end of $410 million, the second half must produce about $239 million; to reach $420 million, about $249 million. That implies roughly $120\u2013125 million per quarter in H2, a step up from Q2's $99.3 million. So the guidance requires a real acceleration, not just continuation. **Bullish thesis by horizon.** - **1 Month:** Momentum and a fresh guidance raise support the stock. The screen pattern \"Up / cooling\" says the move is strong but maturing, so consolidation is possible, but there is no reported negative company news to contradict the demand trend. - **3 Month:** The next quarterly report is the first test of the implicit H2 ramp. If revenue tracks toward $120 million-plus per quarter and losses keep narrowing, the bull case holds. Operating leverage is visible in Q2: revenue rose 66% while the net loss shrank more than half. - **1 Year:** Improving manufacturing and durable Amtagvi demand could push revenue above the new guide as capacity scales. The main unknown is whether the company can show demand or pipeline value beyond advanced melanoma; that evidence is not in the retained material. **Bearish thesis by horizon.** - **1 Month:** After a 543% one-year gain and a >31% guidance rally, the near-term positive news is likely already in the price. The \"cooling\" pattern and the Oct 14 down close are consistent with momentum fading. - **3 Month:** Any sign of manufacturing or collection-rate friction, or a quarter below the new implied pace, would be a negative surprise against elevated expectations. - **1 Year:** The company still burns cash, has no proven path to profitability in evidence, and faces competition in cell therapy. Dilution from future financing is a live risk if the cash burn persists. The bull case beyond current approved use lacks supporting evidence in this research. **Which thesis the facts favor.** The reported facts favor the bullish case on the 1\u20133 month horizon: raised guidance, 66% revenue growth, narrowing losses, and manufacturing improvement are all concrete and current. The bear case is not invalidated, but its strongest point at 1\u20133 months is valuation after a very large run. At one year, neither thesis has a clear edge: the commercial trend is real, but evidence for the pipeline, cash runway, and durable demand outside the current indication is missing. The next earnings report is the key checkpoint for both sides.",
